        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Structure <b>A</b> contains pale discs of tissue, <b>C</b>, that can germinate into new <i>L. cruciata.</i> The new plants that develop from <b>C</b> are genetically identical to the parent plant in Fig. 5.1.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 10
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Structure <b>B</b> contains male sperm that are chemically attracted to swim to female eggs on a neighbouring parent plant. When the egg and sperm fuse, they form structure <b>D</b>. Structure <b>D</b> develops to produce spores that grow into new plants that are genetically different from the two parent plants.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 10
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Identify which of the structures <b>A</b>, <b>B</b>, <b>C</b> and <b>D</b> are:",
            "source": {
              "qp": 10
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "answerLines",
            "labels": [
              "associated with sexual reproduction",
              "produced by mitosis",
              "the site of meiosis"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each letter may be used once, more than once, or not at all.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "marks": 3,
